---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Security - Fable">
  <div class="content-page">
    <h1>Security Architecture</h1>
    <p class="lead">Built to run locally, fail closed, and secure your credentials.</p>
    
    <div class="card">
      <p>Our security design is grounded in these key areas:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Local Execution</strong>: All computations, search indexes, and memory stores remain local.</li>
        <li><strong>OS Keychain Integration</strong>: Raw credentials/API keys never enter JavaScript memory; they are stored in the OS-level credential store.</li>
        <li><strong>Fail-Closed Connectors</strong>: Integrations fail closed unless explicit, single-use approval permits are granted.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>For threat analysis, please inspect <code>docs/security/threat-model.md</code> in the repository.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
